    <!--*-->
    <description>Console Gui library for .net</description>
    <!--*-->
    <releaseNotes>1.3.0
The console can be resized while the application runs. A viewport that is on screen is drawn again for the new size.
- A negative Width or Height of a control (relative to the console) is kept as it was set, and follows the console. Before it was turned into a fixed number when it was set.
- TextArea wraps its text again when its width changes, and does not fail for a very narrow width.
- Picklist keeps the selected item visible when its height changes. ListHeight is public.
- Header, Footer and Input rows shorten text that is longer than the window, instead of wrapping to the next line.
- New: Viewport.RefreshOnResize, Viewport.Resizing, Viewport.Resized and ConsoleWrapper.Resized.
- Breaking: the Viewport constructor no longer changes the size of the console window, set Viewport.Width and Height for that.

1.2.1
Fixed scrolling past the max pages count. Still some quirks, needs testing.

1.2.0 
Changes in IScrollable class to support custom scroll char.</releaseNotes>
